```go
if nowTs-metrics.ts.Load() > b.metricExpireInterval {
    // seed
} else {
    // EWMA
}
```

It should seed only when the previous sample has expired (`now - ts > metricExpireInterval`) or never existed (`ts == 0`). The doc says outright that `0` can't be the "unseeded" marker, because 0 is a normal `ServiceTime` for the sub-millisecond workloads this fix targets.

